  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Initially on increasing temperature rate of reaction will increase, so  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math>  yield will also increase with time. But at equilibrium  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math>  yield at high temperature  <math><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></math>  would be less than at  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math>  as reaction is exothermic so the graph is<br > <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image61-3a64762b-68ca-4eaa-9009-4370647a3a61.jpg\"/></p>",
